{"body":{"children":[{"$ref":"#/texts/0"},{"$ref":"#/texts/1"},{"$ref":"#/texts/2"},{"$ref":"#/texts/3"},{"$ref":"#/texts/4"},{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},{"$ref":"#/texts/29"},{"$ref":"#/texts/30"},{"$ref":"#/texts/31"},{"$ref":"#/texts/32"}],"content_layer":"body","label":"unspecified","name":"_root_","self_ref":"#/body"},"form_items":[],"furniture":{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"unspecified","name":"_root_","self_ref":"#/furniture"},"groups":[],"key_value_items":[],"name":"7eb034036cd99875fe3bea03ccfc11a0f70776d89ed4bf7f644120f84483df1e","origin":{"binary_hash":18131874265165393363,"filename":"7eb034036cd99875fe3bea03ccfc11a0f70776d89ed4bf7f644120f84483df1e.pdf","mimetype":"application/pdf"},"pages":{"1":{"page_no":1,"size":{"height":792.0,"width":612.0}}},"pictures":[{"annotations":[],"captions":[{"$ref":"#/texts/5"}],"children":[{"$ref":"#/texts/5"},{"$ref":"#/texts/6"},{"$ref":"#/texts/7"},{"$ref":"#/texts/8"},{"$ref":"#/texts/9"},{"$ref":"#/texts/10"},{"$ref":"#/texts/11"},{"$ref":"#/texts/12"},{"$ref":"#/texts/13"},{"$ref":"#/texts/14"},{"$ref":"#/texts/15"},{"$ref":"#/texts/16"},{"$ref":"#/texts/17"},{"$ref":"#/texts/18"},{"$ref":"#/texts/19"},{"$ref":"#/texts/20"},{"$ref":"#/texts/21"},{"$ref":"#/texts/22"},{"$ref":"#/texts/23"},{"$ref":"#/texts/24"},{"$ref":"#/texts/25"},{"$ref":"#/texts/26"},{"$ref":"#/texts/27"},{"$ref":"#/texts/28"}],"content_layer":"body","footnotes":[],"label":"picture","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":218.321533203125,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":135.5187225341797,"r":547.29296875,"t":450.62249755859375},"charspan":[0,0],"page_no":1}],"references":[],"self_ref":"#/pictures/0"}],"schema_name":"DoclingDocument","tables":[],"texts":[{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"A thin-provisioned volume feature that is called zero detect provides clients with the ability to reclaim unused allocated disk space (zeros) when they are converting a fully allocated volume to a thin-provisioned volume by using volume mirroring.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":687.2786639999999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.79997599999996,"r":545.3093760000002,"t":723.12318},"charspan":[0,247],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"A thin-provisioned volume feature that is called zero detect provides clients with the ability to reclaim unused allocated disk space (zeros) when they are converting a fully allocated volume to a thin-provisioned volume by using volume mirroring."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.12  Host attachment planning","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":644.03628,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":64.8,"r":301.1340840000001,"t":658.7992800000001},"charspan":[0,30],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"3.12  Host attachment planning"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The typical FC host attachment to the Storwize V7000 is done through SAN fabric. However, the system allows direct attachment connectivity between its 8 Gb or 16 Gb Fibre Channel ports and host ports. No special configuration is required for host systems that are using this configuration. However, the maximum number of directly attached hosts is severely limited by the number of FC ports on Storwize V7000's nodes.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":569.2590479999999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":547.6659359999995,"t":626.4712800000001},"charspan":[0,417],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"The typical FC host attachment to the Storwize V7000 is done through SAN fabric. However, the system allows direct attachment connectivity between its 8 Gb or 16 Gb Fibre Channel ports and host ports. No special configuration is required for host systems that are using this configuration. However, the maximum number of directly attached hosts is severely limited by the number of FC ports on Storwize V7000's nodes."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The Storwize V7000 imposes no particular limit on the distance between the Storwize V7000 nodes and host servers. However, for host attachment, the Storwize V7000 supports up to three ISL hops in the fabric. This capacity means that the server to the Storwize V7000 can be separated by up to five FC links, four of which can be 10 km long (6.2 miles) if long wave Small Form-factor Pluggables (SFPs) are used.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":499.3000079999999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":547.3213200000007,"t":556.51224},"charspan":[0,409],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The Storwize V7000 imposes no particular limit on the distance between the Storwize V7000 nodes and host servers. However, for host attachment, the Storwize V7000 supports up to three ISL hops in the fabric. This capacity means that the server to the Storwize V7000 can be separated by up to five FC links, four of which can be 10 km long (6.2 miles) if long wave Small Form-factor Pluggables (SFPs) are used."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Figure 3-9 shows an example of a supported configuration with Storwize V7000 nodes using shortwave SFPs.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":465.2806319999999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":547.3243080000003,"t":486.49343999999985},"charspan":[0,104],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Figure 3-9 shows an example of a supported configuration with Storwize V7000 nodes using shortwave SFPs."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Figure 3-9   Example of host connectivity","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":206.75700000000006,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":299.14020000000005,"t":215.082},"charspan":[0,41],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Figure 3-9   Example of host connectivity"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Host","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/